      "type": "subjective",
      "section": "Section B",
      "marks": 2,
      "question": "If $P(A) = 3/5$ and $P(B) = 1/5$, find $P(A \\text{ or } B)$ if A and B are independent events.",
      "finalAnswer": "17/25",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "For independent events, $P(A \\cap B) = P(A)P(B) = \\frac{3}{5} \\times \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{3}{25}$.",
        "$P(A \\cup B) = P(A) + P(B) - P(A \\cap B)$.",
        "$= \\frac{3}{5} + \\frac{1}{5} - \\frac{3}{25} = \\frac{4}{5} - \\frac{3}{25} = \\frac{20-3}{25} = \\frac{17}{25}$."
      ]
    },
