      "marks": 4,
      "question": "<strong>Case Study:</strong> In a class of 60 students, 30 opted for NCC, 32 opted for NSS and 24 opted for both NCC and NSS. One student is selected at random.<br>(i) Find the probability that the student opted for NCC or NSS.<br>(ii) Find the probability that the student opted for neither NCC nor NSS.<br>(iii) Find the probability that the student opted for NSS but not NCC.",
      "finalAnswer": "(i) 19/30, (ii) 11/30, (iii) 2/15",
      "solutionSteps": [
        "Total = 60. $n(A)=30, n(B)=32, n(A \\cap B)=24$.",
        "(i) $P(A \\cup B) = \\frac{30+32-24}{60} = \\frac{38}{60} = \\frac{19}{30}$.",
        "(ii) $P(\\text{Neither}) = 1 - P(A \\cup B) = 1 - \\frac{19}{30} = \\frac{11}{30}$.",
        "(iii) $P(B - A) = P(B) - P(A \\cap B) = \\frac{32}{60} - \\frac{24}{60} = \\frac{8}{60} = \\frac{2}{15}$."
      ]
